\name{cellucid_filter_outlier}
\alias{cellucid_filter_outlier}
\title{Filter outliers}
\usage{
cellucid_filter_outlier(viewer, field, threshold)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{field}{The categorical column the view in focus is coloured by, by name. A named list. Required. \describe{\item{\code{key}}{The column name as the app shows it. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}\item{\code{source}}{Categories belong to columns of the cells. Exactly \code{"obs"}. Required.}}}
\item{threshold}{The quantile above which cells are hidden; 1 hides none. A number (at least 0, at most 1). Required.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
Hide the cells of each category that lie furthest from it in the latent space: those above the threshold quantile (1 hides none).
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{filter.outlier} (Filters). It changes the viewer's state: one step of the viewer's history, labelled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{filters}.
